===Etymology===
{{PIE word|en|tréyes}}
From {{inh|en|enm|thirde}}, {{m|enm|thridde}}, from {{inh|en|ang|þridda}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*þridjô}}, from {{pre-Germanic}} {{m|ine-pro||*tret-i(H)-ón-}} or {{m|ine-pro||*trit-i(H)-ón-}}, perhaps a remodeling of {{der|en|ine-pro|*tr̥tyós||third|ng=[[ordinal number]]}}, similar to that in the cognates {{cog|la|tertius}}, {{cog|sa|तृतीय|tr=tṛtī́ya}}, {{cog|ae|𐬚𐬭𐬌𐬙𐬌𐬌𐬀}}{{,}} and {{cog|ine-bsl-pro|*tretjas}} (all {{mg|third (in order)}}), or alternatively some or all of these are from {{m|ine-pro||*trét-yo-}} ~ {{m|ine-pro||*tért-yo-}}, from a distinct root {{m|ine-pro||*ter-t-|third}} from even earlier {{m|ine-pro|*ter-}}; compare {{cog|hit|𒋼𒊑𒀸|tr=te-ri-aš|ts=teryas}}; see {{l|ine-pro|*tritós}} for details. Ultimately from the same root as {{m|en|three}}.

